Press-Outreach/
to-be-integrated/treaties/
Worldspace/Characters/Dolls/**/Reference_Images/*
# Exception: keep the two z-template Reference_Images folders trackable via a .gitkeep placeholder.
# Without this, these folders are always empty (templates have no actual images), and git never
# tracks empty directories at all — so they vanish on any operation that resets the working tree
# to match git's committed state (branch switches, `git clean`, a fresh clone, etc.), forcing them
# to be manually recreated over and over. Real dolls' actual Reference_Images files stay ignored.
!Worldspace/Characters/Dolls/Still-Present_-_In-Game/z-template/Reference_Images/.gitkeep
!Worldspace/Characters/Dolls/Past_History_-_Known_to_Tepenians/z-template/Reference_Images/.gitkeep
Worldspace/Factions/basis collection - robot religions/**/*.mp4
Worldspace/Factions/basis collection - robot religions/**/*.m4a
Reference/Materials/books/*
to-be-integrated/books/*
Repo_Text_Size_Log.md

# graphify build artifacts — machine-specific (absolute paths), regenerable.
# The build plan is kept: it is the resume contract.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/BUILD_PLAN.md

# Third-party copyrighted research PDFs — retained locally for reference, NOT redistributable.
# Same reasoning as Reference/Materials/books/ above. The ASCE paper in here is explicitly stamped
# "Copyright ASCE. For personal use only; all rights reserved." Cite the originals; don't ship them.
# The folder's README.md IS tracked on purpose — it carries the extracted figures (the MCAA factor
# values, the EPA staffing curve) and the register of sources located-but-not-obtained. Those are
# our own notes, and they are the part a future session actually needs.
Reference/Real-World/Industry_Staffing_and_Productivity/*.pdf
